Mandatory part:

• The executable will be named ft_traceroute.

• You must code in C and turn-in a Makefile (respecting the usual rules).

• The only option you’ll have to manage is ––help.

• You have to solely manage a simple IPv4 (address/hostname) as a program parameter.

• You have to manage the FQDN without running the DNS resolution in the jump display.

• A 30ms +/- difference on a jump will be tolerated.

• You are not allowed to set your socket(s) in O_NONBLOCK mode.

• For your mandatory part, you are allowed to use the whole C standard library (the
libC), and nothing but the libC. You may of course still use your own libft and the
printf type functions.

